Unreleased

- Clean up and improve CI config
- Improve --upn help text
- Bugfix: reject --upn when --use-service-account is not given;
  userPrincipalName is an identity attribute and has no business being
  set on a computer account
- Bugfix: add a connect timeout when probing domain controller
  availability, instead of blocking for the OS-level TCP connect
  timeout on an unreachable DC (#220)
- Behavior change: default computer account name now uses only the first DNS
  label of the hostname, matching the hostname selection used by Samba's
  "net ads join", instead of stripping the realm suffix and joining any
  remaining subdomain labels with hyphens (#230)
- Bugfix: an explicitly supplied --hostname was silently re-resolved via
  DNS (if dns_canonicalize_hostname is enabled) and always lowercased,
  instead of being used verbatim; neither Samba's "net ads join" nor
  adcli does this to an explicitly supplied hostname
- Bugfix: "create" unconditionally added the default host/ service
  principal to a machine account, even when --service was given;
  restore skipping the default once --service is explicitly given,
  as documented
- Bugfix: the short form of an unqualified service principal on a
  machine account was derived by truncating the hostname at the
  first dot, instead of using the account's own (NetBIOS) name;
  distinct machine accounts whose hostnames happen to share a
  leading label (e.g. proxy.example.com and
  proxy.loadbalancer.example.com) could register colliding host/
  SPNs even though their account names differ (#136)
- Improvement: support enterprise principals (UPNs whose suffix differs
  from the local realm) when building keytab entries and computing the
  salt (#104, #147)
- Bugfix: "flush" mode's keytab-side cleanup only ever matched a
  machine account's own host/<hostname> SPN; it never removed anything
  for service accounts, and left other SPN aliases on a machine
  account untouched
- Bugfix: "delete" mode left the account's keytab entries behind;
  re-creating an account with the same name could then pick up stale,
  dead keys from the deleted account (#207)
- Bugfix: a servicePrincipalName read back from AD as "HOST/..." (as
  Windows itself writes it) was never normalized to msktutil's own
  "host/..." convention outside of the regular update path, so
  "delete"/"flush" could fail to match and purge such an entry from
  the keytab
- Improvement: "flush" now resets a machine account's keytab and
  servicePrincipalName in AD back to the default sAMAccountName and
  host/ principals, instead of wiping them -- removing them entirely
  would leave the account unreachable over Kerberos by any client.
  userPrincipalName, if set, is always left untouched by "flush"
- Bugfix: an enctype requested via --enctypes, or already present in
  msDs-supportedEncryptionTypes/userAccountControl, that the local
  Kerberos library can no longer use (DES, most commonly -- removed
  entirely from MIT krb5 1.18 onwards, and disabled by default in
  Heimdal) crashed with an uncaught exception mid-run, after already
  changing the account's password and/or servicePrincipalName, leaving
  no usable keytab at all. Fail with a clear error before making any
  change instead. The msktutil-computed default for an account with no
  msDs-supportedEncryptionTypes set at all also no longer includes DES,
  matching what AD/the KDC itself assumes in that case (#172)
- Bugfix: a password change (create/update/auto-update/precreate/reset)
  could be sent to a domain controller other than the one msktutil
  resolved and used for LDAP/authentication; the generated krb5.conf
  pinned kdc/admin_server to the chosen server but never kpasswd_server,
  so the Kerberos library fell back to its own independent DNS SRV
  lookup for the password-change service, bypassing --server/--site
  entirely. This is the root cause of #67 when --server names a
  writable domain controller: LDAP account creation and kinit already
  used that DC correctly, only the password change was silently
  resolved elsewhere (#67)
- Improvement: add --remove-unknown (create/update/auto-update) to
  remove keytab entries for principals this account no longer has in
  AD, e.g. a service principal removed outside of msktutil -- such an
  entry was never revisited by the normal update path and could sit in
  the keytab indefinitely, and could be picked up ahead of the real
  account principal by tools that use the keytab's first entry (e.g.
  kinit -i)
- Bugfix: Makefile.in derived OBJECTS from SOURCES_CPP/SOURCES_C via a
  $(VAR:.ext=.o) substitution reference, a GNU make extension not
  understood by vendor make (e.g. HP-UX's); OBJECTS ended up empty and
  the build failed outright ("Don't know how to make msktutil") on any
  platform without GNU make installed. List the object files
  explicitly instead

Release 1.2.2

